---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How does my son or daughter join Cub Scouts?',
    answer: `Joining is easy! Just bring your child to one of our Pack or Den meetings and one of our leaders will introduce them to the group and help them meet new friends. You will be given a short form to fill out and pay the annual Pack dues. You can also email the Cubmaster at <a href="mailto:cubmaster@pack3472.org">cubmaster@pack3472.org</a>.`,
  },
  {
    question: 'What do I need to buy for my son or daughter to get started?',
    answer: `The Scout Store is located at <strong>10210 Holmes Road, Kansas City, MO</strong> inside the Boy Scouts' Heart of America Council building. Your scout will need: 1) Blue uniform shirt, 2) scarf and slide for their rank, 3) patches, 4) belt, and 5) handbook for their rank.`,
  },
  {
    question: "What's a Pack and what's a Den?",
    answer: `In Cub Scouts, the large group of boys and girls from Kindergarten through 5th grade is called a <strong>Pack</strong>. The Pack is broken down into smaller groups by age (rank) called <strong>Dens</strong>. Dens meet on their own once a month to work on age-appropriate skills and activities together.`,
  },
  {
    question: "What if my son or daughter plays sports and has other activities?",
    answer: `We encourage all of our scouts to be well-rounded and to participate in other activities! We understand that your kids will have conflicts and miss meetings from time to time — and that's OK. Talk to your Den Leader and we will help your scout catch up on requirements they missed.`,
  },
  {
    question: 'Can siblings come to Pack and Den activities?',
    answer: `Absolutely! We are a family-centered Pack and siblings are always welcome. If siblings are not old enough to follow along, please bring a quiet activity for them during times when the scouts need to listen.`,
  },
  {
    question: "My scout is going to miss a meeting! Now what?",
    answer: `Relax. Check with your Den Leader to see if they missed any requirements, then catch up at home or at a later time. Missing an occasional meeting is no big deal.`,
  },
  {
    question: "My son or daughter didn't join in kindergarten. Can they still join now?",
    answer: `Yes! Your scout can join at any point between Kindergarten and 5th grade. They do <strong>not</strong> need to complete requirements from earlier grades first; they start at their grade-appropriate rank and move forward from there.`,
  },
];
---

<Layout title="FAQ" description="Frequently asked questions about joining BSA Cub Scout Pack 3472 in Leawood, KS.">
  <h1 class="page-title">Pack 3472 FAQ's</h1>
  <hr class="rule" />

  <p>
    Below is a list of commonly asked questions. If your question isn't covered here, feel free to send us an email
    through the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
  </p>

  {faqs.map((faq) => (
    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>{faq.question}</h3>
      <p set:html={faq.answer} />
    </article>
  ))}
</Layout>
